  "worked_solution": "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={\u222c}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={\u222c}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{M}{6}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}({\\int }_{-1}^{2}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{3}(x+1)^{3}]_{-1}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(\\frac{1}{3}(2+1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(-1+1)^{3})\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(9-0)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3M.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
